Turbo exports VM image and installer helpers independently of its NixOS modules: let library = turbo.lib.hypervisor { inherit pkgs; };
in { # Example values for a consumer's VM configuration: diskImage = library.qcow2.debian_13_trixie_genericcloud; seedImage = library.cloud-config { meta_data = "instance-id: example-vm\nlocal-hostname: example-vm\n"; user_data = '' #cloud-config users: - name: operator ssh_authorized_keys: - ssh-ed25519 AAAA...replace-with-your-public-key ''; network_config = '' version: 2 ethernets: eth0: dhcp4: true ''; };
} For a non-flake import, use (import /path/to/turbo/lib).hypervisor { inherit pkgs; }. The caller supplies pkgs, so helpers use the caller's nixpkgs revision, overlays, and build platform. Importing the library neither enables services nor downloads images. There is no overlay or NixOS module argument to configure.
